# The Samsung MDFPP key chain (libbauthtzcommon.so -> BAuth_GetK_From_KM)
# falls back to the QTI keymaster path and looks for the TA under the name
# "keymaster64"; the APNHLOS firmware partition only ships "skeymast".
# QSEECom resolves the app by file name, so provide an alias.
# /vendor/firmware_mnt is a real (persistent) partition, so this only runs
# once per flash, but the check keeps it idempotent.
on post-fs-data
    exec - root system -- /system/bin/sh /vendor/bin/fp_fw_alias.sh
